("h2","The idea of priority"),
("p","When a company can't pay everyone, creditors are paid in a set order. Secured lenders are generally ahead of unsecured creditors, who are ahead of shareholders. Restructuring interviews often test this order, sometimes through a recovery waterfall (see <a href=\"/guides/restructuring-interview-questions/\">restructuring interview questions</a>)."),
("h2","Is it a good career?"),
("p","Restructuring work tends to pick up when the economy is under stress, and the deals are often complex and fast-moving. People in this field often learn a lot about debt and legal structure, which is helpful for credit investing and private equity too."),
("h2","Common questions"),
("qa","Do I need to know law?","No, but you need to understand the basics of bankruptcy and how debt is ranked. Lawyers handle the legal side."),
("qa","What skills do I need?","Strong accounting, a good understanding of debt, comfort with models and the ability to communicate clearly under pressure."),
("qa","Is restructuring only busy in recessions?","Activity usually rises in tough times, but companies also restructure debt for other reasons, so the work is not limited to recessions."),
